    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really sharp way to put it. it makes the opposition look pretty naive. i'm also seeing a lot of noise from the fiscal conservatives who just keep bringing up inflation and the massive cost of the program. it feels like they're just stuck in an old-school mindset that doesn't account for the massive productivity gains ai will bring. how can i effectively dismiss those fiscal concerns as being economically shortsighted or irrelevant in an automated future?",
